    "note": "the tracks are the escape from each land.  The pours were added after the routing, so every track crossing an outline slits it: measured, they recover between a fortieth and two thirds of their own outline area (fill.json).  They are extra copper in parallel with the escapes, not a plane, and this layout should not be quoted as a 10 A conductor -- IPC-2221 at 1 oz and a 10 degC rise puts 10 A at about 7 mm of conductor.  Those ampacity numbers are a chart, quoted to say what the copper is not; they are not a measurement, a thermal model or a rating.  VSS is routed at signal width on purpose: it is the controller's source reference through the R1 Kelvin tap, not a current path."
