    "route with the pours in mind: measured in fill.json, the fills recover between 2.5 % and 64 % of their own outline because the routing came first and every track crossing an outline slits it.  The secondary corridors show it worst: SEC_B keeps 2.5 % of 360 mm2 and contains one of the lands it serves (J3.3, whose centre sits on the outline edge), SEC_A keeps 10.7 % and contains no land centre at all -- it joins the net through the tracks the fill touches.  So each corridor is a strip beside a 0.8 mm escape, not a conductor.  Either re-route with the pour corridors kept clear of signal copper, or go to four layers and use an inner plane; until then the current path is the escapes",
